{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>One thing</b> — It seems to me that David composed this psalm at the end of his days, when his men swore: 'You shall not go with us to battle,' as I will explain in the psalm 'YHWH said to my master' [Psalm 110]." "<b>To behold the pleasantness of YHWH</b> — That secrets of the Creator's work be revealed to him, which he had not known until now." "<b>And to visit His temple</b> — like 'he shall not distinguish between good and bad' [Genesis 31:29, לא יבקר]; the meaning is that the priests who sit constantly in the House would teach him and give him to drink." "Others say: <b>to visit</b> — to go every morning into the temple of HaShem, like: 'early and late' [the root בקר as 'morning']."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:48.661068846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}